	(descr "Resonant bank film capacitor, dual-pitch 2-pin radial (native-21 stage 51, DECISIONS 73): one RES_A-side pad 1 at 0 and two pad-2 holes, at 22.5 mm (TDK B32643B8104J000, the 28 A alternate, not fitted) and at 27.5 mm (KNSCHA MMK104J3DF1KN208G2, fitted). The two pad-2 holes share the number, so both are on the SW_B net and the unused one stays open (plated, no lead). FITTED: KNSCHA MMKP82 104J2000V P=27.5, spec KNS20200505002 (LCSC C528962, sha256 4621763054ad5e92...) p.3 dimensions: W 31.5 +-0.5, H 19.5 +-0.5, T 11 +-0.5, P 27.5 +-0.5, d 0.8 +-0.05 mm; body at its maximum 32 x 11.5 x 20 mm, centred on the 27.5 mm pitch (x -2.25 .. 29.75). ALTERNATE: TDK B3264*B data sheet (6/26, sha256 ab9fdca0...4a58ab77) p.2 e 22.5 +-0.4 mm, d1 0.8 +-0.05 mm; p.11 maximum body 14.5 x 29.5 x 26.5 mm, centred on the 22.5 mm pitch (x -2.0 .. 24.5). Drill 1.2 mm for the 0.8 mm leads of both parts (0.85 mm max lead; JLC PTH drill tolerance +0.13 / -0.08 mm leaves >= 0.27 mm diametral clearance); pad 2.4 mm, annular ring 0.6 mm against JLC's 'PTH annular ring, Multilayer 2 oz' >= 0.254 mm (FAB-JLCPCB.md). F.Fab: both maximum bodies. F.SilkS and F.CrtYd: one rectangle around the union (courtyard 0.5 mm beyond it along X, 0.2 mm across, as the stage-49 bank, which stacks at 15.0 mm pitch). Origin at pin 1. Pad 1 is round like pad 2 (neither part has polarity): a square pad 1 corner of the row-5 cap came 8.035 mm (plan view) from the In1 v3v3 plane corner at (159.9, 122.2) on stage 49, under the 8.047 mm HOT-SELV minimum; round, 8.325 mm. 3D model: the fitted KNSCHA body; the TDK alternate's model is models3d/capacitors/TDK_B32643B8104J000.step (same origin, swap the model path to view it).")
